        "sha256": "fac30df6e3f8355ba5d8529b65aa7af05f87247c6eeaf36176beaba1b27b58a7",
        "change": "Only final failed-run FOS publication and summary formatting; constitutive and solver algorithms unchanged from INCO_14."
      },
      {
        "build": "20261009_INCO_16",
        "sha256": "a4c4ca06c794fc3128175a04bdd50eef2a6694914d0a56747a8bdf6597841db7",
        "change": "Preserve the nonfatal deferred Fs=1 gravity failure until SRM classifies it, enabling the intended Fs<1 search. Numerical acceptance criteria and material laws unchanged."
      },
      {
        "build": "20261009_INCO_21",
        "sha256": "65489c15a5bdd9716ba49c1a78489e6e6ca64d16039298ab2834b3e33a20eacd",
        "change": "Refine nonsymmetric band LU against the original CSR residual; bounded residual recovery and elastic correction retry. INCONSISTENT SRM uses material internal forces and their Newton tangent; hourglass stiffness is only an elastic correction regularizer. Material stress law, psi and acceptance tolerances unchanged. Exact-value CSR factor cache is invalidated on any matrix change."
      },
      {
        "build": "20261010_INCO_22",
        "sha256": "90aa723795ee025f88035cf4e45e20000f003979da992bd7a4be5072809db13e",
        "change": "Extend the INCO21 elastic-correction retry to seed gravity and replay in an SRM-enabled stage plan. Previously it was restricted to running SRM trials. The same physical force residual, material law, stopping tolerances and bounded retry apply. Other solver paths are unchanged."
      },
      {
        "build": "20261010_INCO_23",
        "sha256": "27b949ab8e186b6398f604c15a4ad99c89a3d1ab33ff7a7a82128d121650d777",
        "change": "Carry a successful elastic correction between increments within one SRM-enabled load stage. On failure restore committed state and retry full Newton once. Each target uses at most one attempt per correction mode; stage/function entry resets preference. Force/yield laws, tolerances and solver kernels unchanged from INCO22."
      },
      {
        "build": "20261010_INCO_24",
        "sha256": "83b1e4d527c0a9920603d052743df829abc552a582d319e29f20f8776a132856",
        "change": "Release the elastic-correction preference after a slow (>100 iterations) or tiny-progress (<5% of initial stage increment) success, then start the next target with full Newton. The bounded two-mode retry and physical acceptance criteria are unchanged from INCO23."
      }
    ],
    "scope": "Dry or total-stress homogeneous plane-strain slopes. No hydraulic coupling or post-collapse travel.",
